generateModelBySelections()  (or generateModelByPrompt())
  └─ active regenerationContext { modelId, modelVersionId }
       ├─ originalModelData = modelEditorStore.getSerializedData()
       │    (the current XML already has <dbpm:info> from its creation)
       │
       ├─ generateModel(input) → LLM returns fresh raw process XML
       │
       └─ composeRegeneratedModelData({ currentModelData, generatedModelData, selectionUpdate })
            ├─ extracts the new <description> payload from fresh LLM XML
            │
            ├─ if currentModelData has dbpm wrapper:
            │    replaces the inner <description> inside the existing wrapper
            │    (preserving all <dbpm:info> metadata from original)
            │
            └─ updateDbpmTextSelections(serialized, selectedText, meta)   ← INJECTION UPDATE
                 • finds existing <dbpm:document_info> via ensureDbpmPath()
                 • upserts <dbpm:text_selections> ← new selection text
                 • upserts <dbpm:prompt>          ← new prompt (if any)
                 • upserts documentVersionId / documentVersionName (if in meta)
                 • returns updated serialized XML  (regeneratedDataXml)

       → preview = { originalDataXml, regeneratedDataXml, updateType }

       if context still active:
         modelEditorStore.setData(regeneratedDataXml, { updateType })
         setRegenerationDraftEditingModel()
           → editingModel = { id, versionId: null, sourceVersionId }
           → state = "regeneration-draft"
         → #regenerationDraftReviewBar becomes visible

  User clicks Replace    → updateEditingVersion()  (saves regeneratedDataXml over existing version)
  User clicks Save new  → createModelVersion()     (creates new version from regeneratedDataXml)
  User clicks Cancel    → restores originalDataXml, resets editingModel